    feat: add docs-count-drift failure class. Addresses LORE-032.
    
    One new curated class in the closed SEED_CLASSES registry so docs/count-drift
    phrasings ("docs still cite the old test count", "README claims 293 tests but
    the suite has 301") classify instead of falling back to unclassified. Scope is
    docs/count drift only — runbook placeholder lint, validator refusal, and
    fresh-clone pytest vocabularies stay out by design (near-miss guard test pins
    gateway-drain-window unaffected).
    
    - lore/classes.py: docs-count-drift seed entry (signature patterns, keywords,
      provenance citing LORE-019/025/028/029 + the count-sync doctrine).
    - lore/compiler.py: checks / recovery ladder / guardrails / evidence trail for
      the new class, following the LORE-017 per-class shape. Check 1 uses a
      gate-approvable python3 -c collect-only form (default-deny gate untouched).
    - tests/test_classifier.py: stress phrase, count-mismatch variant, token-exact
      matched_signature, and the gateway near-miss overreach guard.
    - tests/test_classes.py + tests/test_lore017_gateway_guard.py: registry count
      pin DERIVED from SEED_CLASSES instead of hardcoded == 11 (LORE-017
      precedent); SEED_CLASS_IDS list gains the missing gateway-guard-violation
      entry so the derived pin stays exact.
    - README.md / docs/INSTALL.md / skills/lore-usage/SKILL.md /
      scripts/test-count.txt: count literals 293 → 297 and "10 curated classes" →
      11 — the count-sync guard caught the drift and these land in the same
      commit, per LORE-029 doctrine.
    
    Verified: uv run pytest -q (297 passed), ruff check + format --check clean,
    lore match stress phrase → docs-count-drift confidence=0.90, lore audit lists
    the new class, count-sync guard PASS (canonical=297 matches live=297).
